004 science fiction blockbuster  irobot  she portrayed susan calvin a  robo-psychologist who helps robot hating  detective del spooner  played by will smith investigate a death  that might have been caused by a robot  unfortunately robots repeatedly attack  the pair  as they investigate and they eventually  uncover a much larger conspiracy  in the form of a plot by a rogue central  computer  only a few elements of the film i robot  are based on isaac asimov's collection  of short stories  of the same name but moynihan's role is  one of them  the character appeared in much of  asimov's robot themed fiction  serving as chief robo psychologist at  the manufacturing company u.s robots and  mechanical men  inc and was often portrayed as a  brilliant if  coldly logical scientist lately the best  place to see moynihan has been on the  cbs procedural drama blue bloods  where she plays aaron the only daughter  of new york city police commissioner  frank reagan  played by tom selleck while her brothers  danny  jamie and the deceased joe followed  their father into the family business of  policing  aaron reagan decided to become a new  york county assistant district attorney  any character on a show that's been  running for 11 seasons will have seen  her fair share of  ups and downs and aaron is no different  she's had a variety of love interests  since divorcing her husband jack boyle  played by peter herman  however some of aaron's potential love  interests were either the district  attorney  or would eventually take on the role  making them her boss  she's watched her daughter nikki played  by sammy gale grow up  multiple times she's had to be saved by  members of her family  meaning that there's never a dull moment  on the show blue blood's  busy network drama schedule which has  seen more than 220 episodes to date  has kept moynihan busy for the better  part of a decade  with her appearing in only a handful of  other film roles during that time  these include battle los a